Let the distance traveled by the plane be $d$ miles and the time taken be $t$ hours. We are given that the plane travels 1200 miles in 3 hours. Therefore, the rate of the plane is
$$ \text{rate} = \frac{\text{distance}}{\text{time}} = \frac{1200 \text{ miles}}{3 \text{ hours}} = 400 \text{ miles per hour} $$
We want to find the additional time it would take to travel an additional 2000 miles at the same rate. Let the additional time be $x$ hours. We have
$$ \text{distance} = \text{rate} \times \text{time} $$
So, the additional distance is $2000 \text{ miles}$ and the rate is $400 \text{ miles per hour}$.
$$ 2000 = 400 \times x $$
$$ x = \frac{2000}{400} = 5 $$
Therefore, it would take 5 additional hours to travel an additional 2000 miles at the same rate.

